course: dictionary
lesson: 10983
title: Warmth: heat and kindness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Warmth is a noun, a thing you can have, and it has two meanings. The first is a gentle heat, like «the warmth of the fire». The second is a friendly, kind feeling towards people, like «She greeted us with warmth.»
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. Ask: is the sentence about temperature, or about how someone feels? Clues such as fire, sun, cold or dough point to heat. Clues such as greeted, kind or safety point to feelings.
explain: «Warmth makes yeast work faster, so dough is left somewhere warm» is about heat, because dough and yeast are things that respond to temperature. Swap in your meaning to check: if you put «gentle heat» in place of warmth and it still makes sense, you have the right one.
fact: Warmth means the state of being warm, a gentle heat.
fact: Warmth also means a friendly, kind feeling towards people.
fact: «Milk left out on a warm table goes sour because bacteria multiply fast in warmth.»
fact: Clothes and fur keep warmth in by trapping air, which is called insulation.
fact: In stories, warmth often shows kindness, love or safety at home.
exercise: «The warmth of the fire spread across the room.» What does warmth mean here? | A cold draught | A friendly welcome from a stranger | * A gentle heat | A loud noise
exercise: «She greeted us with warmth.» What kind of warmth is this? | A thick, woolly jumper | Heat energy in a science lab | * A friendly, kind feeling towards people
exercise: «Clothes and fur keep warmth in by trapping air.» What job does the trapped air do? | It makes the fur turn green | It makes the clothes cold | * It keeps the heat in | It stops us feeling anything at all
test: «Milk left out on a warm table goes sour because bacteria multiply fast in warmth.» What does warmth help the bacteria do? | * Multiply fast | Freeze solid | Turn into butter | Grow fur
test: «In stories, warmth often shows kindness, love or safety at home.» What does warmth usually show in a story? | * Kindness and safety | How fast a clock ticks | The temperature of the weather | How loudly someone talks
exam: Which sentence uses warmth to mean a friendly, kind feeling? | The warmth of the sun on our backs | Dough left somewhere warm | Milk left on a warm table | * She greeted us with warmth
